\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The inversion product}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Let #{H} be a self-adjoint operator on a finite-dimensional complex Hermitian field space. Suppose #{H} preserves its character spaces. Let #{A} be an antiunitary of square #{-\bbI} commuting with #{H} and preserving each self-opposite block. Let #{P} be a complex-linear unitary involution implementing inversion of labels and commuting there with both #{H} and #{A}. For #{r=-r} let #{W^-_r} be the strictly negative spectral subspace of #{H_r}. The \newvocab{inversion product} is
##{\prod_{r=-r}(-1)^{\dim_{\mathbb C}(W^-_r\cap\ker(P+\bbI))/2}.}
The joint subspace is stable under #{A}; the orthogonal-pair argument of \ref{fdip-01AO} makes its dimension even. An empty product is one.}
